The contract:
1. `game.undo()` reverts the most recent turn-costing action. State exactly as before, including rng state, log, monsters, level, depth. Returns true when a turn was undone, false when nothing.
2. Up to 10 turns can be undone in a row; older history discarded.
3. `game.state.undo` holds number of turns that can currently be undone (0 to 10); history stored as `game.state.history`, preserved by serialize/load.
4. `hash()` ignores `history` and `undo` fields. hash before action == hash after undo. Acting again after undo behaves exactly as first time (same rng, same result).
5. `applyKey(game, "z")` calls `undo()` and returns `["You rewind time."]` when undone, `["Nothing to rewind."]` otherwise. `runScript` accepts z.
6. Page: z key rewinds, HUD shows `Undo N`, renderer shows rewound state at once (positions, hp, log, level) with brief visual cue.
7. Add tests and README docs. npm test passes.

